  "notes": [
    "Static string/UUID extraction only. It does not decrypt signed/encrypted firmware.",
    "ATOMOS 9-digit Pairing ID and Android SMP passkey are treated as separate layers.",
    "High-entropy firmware can contain accidental short ASCII collisions. Isolated S1C/BLE/BTPR/UUID fragments are weak evidence unless clustered in a structured executable/string region.",
    "The 17.7 Android build does not send BTPR/S1C ASCII into the proprietary 9383 GATT service without a proven transport mapping.",
    "Use hit.evidence: weak-high-entropy-collision-risk means the token is not protocol proof by itself. Full UUID/magic/string clusters in structured regions are stronger evidence."
  ]
